\paragraph{Paired uncertainty and depth heterogeneity.}
We resample whole skill groups with replacement $10{,}000$ times and
report percentile intervals for paired accuracy differences
(Table~\ref{tab:state-depth-uncertainty}). The Qwen3-8B/MedCalc intervals
reuse the independently audited analysis; the other cells use a fixed
seed of $20261024$. Five cells have positive intervals in both contexts;
Qwen/TheoremQA's Neutral lower endpoint is zero. Llama/TheoremQA and
DeepSeek/MedCalc have mixed point-estimate directions and intervals
including zero in both receivers. Thus these data do not establish either
consistent late-layer superiority in those cells or a universal early-layer
advantage under joint repair. The Qwen3-8B/MedCalc early-minus-late gap
remains $66.1/64.5$ points. Even adversarially scoring its capped outputs
against this contrast leaves $63.7/64.5$ points. Cap counts in the other
cells are reported rather than silently treated as unobserved continuations.
The intervals are exploratory, unadjusted for multiple comparisons, and
some cells have few skill groups.

